    skos:definition "(GER. *Gemälde, Schilder-eyen. Du. Schilderyen. DA. Malerie, Skilderie. Sw. Mälningar. FR. Tableaux. IT. Pitture, Quadri. SP. Pinturas, Cuadros. PORT. Pinturas. RUS. Kartinü. POL. Nalowania.*) The taste for foreign paintings and pictures having lately surprisingly decreased, our inland trade, in the productions of the English school of painting, has experienced a vast augmentation; and it is even said that great quantities of these articles are sent to, and eagerly bought up, on the continent of Europe. See PAINTING. [Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 752]"@en ;
